{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1791119035,"nonce":"jNzx2sGMrbk7bn6WHFKxtlv62Xk=","target":"b0b7728d2153fa147b757de56303a97bd8f77a131721f571a89008da404a30a9","message":"A built-in \u003ccanvas\u003e element with an immediate-mode drawing context, 2D and 3D, rendered on the GPU through ashui's own pipeline. It is the foundation for charts, and for anything else that draws rather than lays out.\n\nThe model is Blinc's canvas element and DrawContext, with blinc_canvas_kit's Painter2D, Sketch, CanvasKit (2D infinite canvas) and SceneKit3D (3D scene viewer) above it. The names follow Blinc's, not HTML's canvas API. It is built Haxe-first, with shaders in hxsl.\n\n- `\u003ccanvas draw={(ctx, bounds) -\u003e ...}\u003e`. `ctx` is a DrawContext:\n  - Transform stack: pushTransform, popTransform.\n  - Clips: pushClip with a rect, rounded rect, circle or path; popClip. Opacity: pushOpacity, popOpacity.\n  - fillRect and strokeRect (with corner radius), fillCircle, strokeCircle.\n  - fillPath and strokePath, taking a Path and a Stroke (width, cap, join, miter limit, dash) and a Brush (solid, linear or radial gradient).\n  - drawText and drawImage later.\n- Path: moveTo, lineTo, quadTo, cubicTo, arcTo, arc, rect, roundedRect, circle, ellipse, close; also built from SVG path data.\n- Reactive in Solid style: `draw` runs inside a tracked computation and runs again only when a signal it read changes. Size changes also redraw it.\n- Painter, after Painter2D: the current fill and stroke, push and pop, rect, roundedRect, circle, line, path.\n- Sketch: `setup` and `draw(ctx, t, dt)` every frame, clocked by AnimationScheduler, so recordings and tests are deterministic. State lives in the sketch object. A Player extension point covers timeline content.\n- 3D in the same context, as in Blinc: setCamera, drawMesh, addLight, setEnvironment. A SceneKit3D-like layer goes above it: an orbit camera, geometry primitives and a material builder.\n\nThe current pipeline has 112-float records drawn as SDF quads, no triangle pipeline, no MSAA and no stencil. The canvas route:\n1. blinc_abi emits one PRIM_CANVAS placeholder record over a canvas node's content box, as image_record does for SVGs, through a `blinc_tree_set_canvas(node, slot)` setter. The placeholder carries the node's transform, clips, fades, clip-path, opacity and layers.\n2. Haxe, at sync time as Images.resolve does, expands each placeholder:\n   - rects, rounded rects and circles become the existing SDF box records;\n   - paths become path records, one per fill or stroke call, carrying the paint and a vertex range. Their triangle vertices are appended to the records texture after the native rows, as clip-path polygon points are.\n3. A PathShader (hxsl, imports Sdf) fetches vertices by vertex index. It places them through the record's affine, and in the fragment applies the paint, the per-vertex fringe coverage and the clip products. Renderer draws each path record non-indexed: renderDrawRange(vertexCount, 1, 0, record).\n\nA depth attachment and a mesh pipeline: vertex and index buffers through hlwgpu's GpuPipelineBuilder attribute and depth support, PBR shading ported from Blinc's mesh pipeline into hxsl, and an orbit camera. The 3D content renders into a layer texture that the canvas placeholder composites, so it sits in paint order and takes clips and opacity.\n\n- Paths are flattened at a tolerance scaled by on-screen scale, so they stay crisp when zoomed.\n- Fills: a convex fast path as a fan, and ear clipping for simple concave polygons and their holes. Neither overlaps, so translucent fills do not double-blend.\n- Strokes are expanded to triangles, with miter, round and bevel joins and butt, round and square caps.\n- Antialiasing is a 1px feathered fringe with coverage per vertex, as NanoVG does, independent of MSAA.\n\n1. Vector core: Path, flattening, fill and stroke tessellation, fringe. Unit tests.\n2. Render plumbing: PRIM_CANVAS, expansion, PathShader. Pixel tests.\n3. \u003ccanvas\u003e element and DrawContext, with reactive redraw. Painter and Sketch. Snapshot and motion scenes.\n4. Charts on top (line, bar, area, pie), in ashui.components.\n5. Text and images in the context.\n6. 3D: depth, the mesh pipeline, camera and lights, then the SceneKit3D layer.\n7. CanvasKit: pan, zoom, spatial hit regions, selection and background patterns.","files":null}]}